# ==============================================================================
# tools/binaryen-native-tools/.gitignore
# ==============================================================================
#
# THE FIRST RULE BELOW ("!*") IS LOAD-BEARING - DO NOT DELETE IT.
#
# The repository-root .gitignore is the standard Visual Studio / .NET one. It
# ignores names that also occur inside the vendored binaryen tree and in this
# folder's own scripts, for example:
#
#     *.env                     -> linux/pins.env
#     *.log  [Oo]ut/  [Ll]og/  [Dd]ebug/  [Rr]elease/  bld/  [Oo]bj/ ...
#     [Ww][Ii][Nn]32/  [Aa][Rr][Mm]64/  *.obj  *.pdb  ...
#
# Without the "!*" below, such files would be silently left out of every
# commit, and the vendored snapshot (or the build pins) would not be there for
# the next person who cloned this repository. A nested .gitignore takes
# precedence over the ones above it, so re-including everything here and then
# re-ignoring only what this folder genuinely produces is the correct fix - and
# it keeps the root .gitignore untouched. (Same rule, same reason, as
# CodeBrix.LibGit2's libgit2-native-tools/.gitignore.)
#
# binaryen/.gitignore is UPSTREAM's own file and part of the unmodified
# snapshot. It is deeper than this one, so it still applies inside binaryen/ -
# which is correct: it only names build products and editor files, and no file
# in the version_133 tarball matches it (see UPSTREAM.txt).
#
# Verify at any time with:
#     git status --ignored --porcelain -- tools/binaryen-native-tools
#         -> should list only output/ and unstripped/ contents (and nothing at
#            all on a clean clone)
# ==============================================================================

# Re-include everything under this folder, overriding the root .gitignore.
!*
!*/

# --- what this folder really does produce, and must not commit ---------------

# Built executables, gate runs, logs, SHA256SUMS. ONE tree, shared by every
# platform build. THE LEADING SLASH MATTERS: without it the pattern would match
# ANY directory named "output" at any depth, including inside binaryen/.
/output/

# The pre-strip executables of the adopted builds, kept on the build machine
# only: the owner decided (2026-11-18) NOT to commit them. Same leading-slash
# rule; the trailing /* (not a bare /unstripped/) lets the README below be
# re-included - a directory that is itself excluded is never descended into.
/unstripped/*
!/unstripped/README.txt

# Finder droppings. Needed explicitly: the "!*" above re-includes everything
# under this folder and so overrides any .DS_Store rule inherited from the root
# or from a user's global gitignore.
.DS_Store
